<Project Sdk="WixToolset.Sdk/5.0.2">
  <!-- URmessage MSI: a per-user install of the Release output folder (see
       Package.wxs). Build it after the solution, from app:
         msbuild installer\Installer.wixproj /restore /p:Configuration=Release /p:Platform=x64
       It lands in installer\bin\<Platform>\<Configuration>\URmessage.msi.
       Check what is inside with tools\verify-msi-payload.ps1.

       Not in URmessage.sln on purpose: the solution builds the app, and this
       project packages what that build produced.

       Directory.Build.props is imported here too (every project under app\
       gets it), and its OutDir is scoped to .vcxproj. That scoping is what
       keeps this MSI out of the folder it installs; see the note there.
       SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputName>URmessage</OutputName>
    <OutputType>Package</OutputType>
    <!-- The folder the app build writes (Directory.Build.props OutDir) and the
         one Package.wxs installs. Override per arch/config on the command
         line. -->
    <BinDir Condition="'$(BinDir)'==''">$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\build\$(Platform)\Release</BinDir>
    <!-- MSI ProductVersion fields are 8.8.16-bit, so the MSI cannot carry the
         app's YYYY.M.D-code version; a stamping build passes
         /p:UrMsiVersion=<major.minor.build> instead. Unstamped, it is 0.0.1,
         matching the code-0 app build the props defaults describe. Same-version
         builds still replace each other: MajorUpgrade in Package.wxs allows
         same-version upgrades, and WiX gives every build a new ProductCode. -->
    <UrMsiVersion Condition="'$(UrMsiVersion)'==''">0.0.1</UrMsiVersion>
    <DefineConstants>BinDir=$(BinDir);UrMsiVersion=$(UrMsiVersion)</DefineConstants>
    <!-- Installer warnings describe install, upgrade and repair correctness,
         not polish, so every one stops the build, except the two ICEs below.
         That includes ICE38, ICE64, ICE91 and ICE105, which this per-user
         package passes rather than suppresses (see the Package.wxs header). -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <!-- ICE03 fails on the harvested Windows App SDK payload, not on anything
         authored here. Un-suppressed, it reports exactly 8 rows (Windows App
         SDK 2.2.0, x64), all in the File table's Language column:
           - String overflow, 2 rows: Microsoft.ui.xaml.dll and
             Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Phone.dll each declare 86 languages (430
             characters), too long a list for the column;
           - Invalid Language Id, 6 rows: the .mui satellites of those two
             dlls in gd-gb (LCID 1169), mi-NZ (1153) and ug-CN (1152), LCIDs
             ICE03's reference table does not know.
         The column is inert here: the package has no transforms or patches,
         and the OS resource loader never reads MSI metadata. The URnetwork VPN
         client suppresses ICE03 for the same runtime and records the same
         reason (its installer/Installer.wixproj). Suppressing ICE03 does not
         suppress ICE60, which still runs on the fonts (authored as companion
         files in Package.wxs).

         WiX can suppress an ICE only for the whole package (wix msi validate
         -sice), not per table or per file, so this also hides ICE03 on what
         Package.wxs authors by hand: the launch conditions, the shortcut's
         Target, the registry value. tools\verify-msi-ice03.ps1 runs ICE03 on
         its own and passes only on exactly the 8 rows above; CI runs it after
         every MSI build. When a Windows App SDK bump changes the rows, update
         the list there and here together.

         ICE61 warns that the upgrade row's maximum version includes this
         package's own version ("The Maximum version is not less than the
         current product"). That is AllowSameVersionUpgrades in Package.wxs,
         on purpose: two builds of one version (every unstamped 0.0.1 build,
         for one) must replace each other rather than install side by side.
         WiX authors that row; nothing here hand-authors Upgrade rows. -->
    <SuppressIces>ICE03;ICE61</SuppressIces>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
